Q: How to set by default selected values in PrimeNg MultiSelect with Angular 4 Reactive Form? A: <p>You need to provide value for your <code>selectedSensorsList</code> when you create the <code>formGroup</code>:</p>

<pre><code> this.addEditWebhookForm = this._formBuilder.group({
     ...,
     selectedSensorsList: [
         defaulSensorsList
     ]
 });
</code></pre>

<p>or set the value later:</p>

<p><code>this._formBuilder.get('selectedSensorsList').setValue(defaultSenorsList);</code></p>

Q: Select&#39;s dropdown direction A: <p>You can see how far the click event is from the top and the bottom by accessing the event object.</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>var pretendSelect = document.querySelector('#pretendSelect');
var daDiv = document.querySelector('#daDiv')

daDiv.addEventListener('click', function(ev){
  
  pretendSelect.style.display = "block";
  pretendSelect.style.left = ev.clientX + 'px';
  
  if(ev.clientY &gt; 120 ){
     pretendSelect.style.top = ev.clientY - 80 + 'px';
  
  } else {
    pretendSelect.style.top = ev.clientY + 'px';
  }
  
  console.log(ev.clientX);
  console.log(ev.clientY);
})</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>#daDiv {
  background:red;
  width:200px;
  height: 200px;
  left:0;
  top:0;
}

#pretendSelect {
  height:80px;
  position:absolute;
  background:blue;
  width:50px;
  z-index:1;
  top:0;
  display:none;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="daDiv"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="pretendSelect"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How to gracefully catch jsonwebtoken errors in node &amp; express? A: <p>May be user is asking how to handle different types of error or how to inform front end user that your login time is over please re login to continue</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>if (err) {
  if (err.name == &quot;TokenExpiredError&quot;) {
    res.json({ message: &quot;Request Timeout Please Re login&quot;});
  }
} else {
  console.log(err);
}
</code></pre>
